--- !u!114 &8749121131333605047
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 4423815028851150653}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a6c638bf07f19cc428b27368804fb218, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuestFlight.Product.Training.TrainingCoach
  training: {fileID: 406945266046702129}
  flight: {fileID: 742791276885309778}
  instrumentProvider: {fileID: 4122695829926210968}
  lines:
  - cue: 1
    reference: 2
    text: The right bank is steep. Turn the yoke gently left to reduce the bank,
      then ease the input.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c476b69c83895d340b2b741962ae0a4d, type: 3}
  - cue: 2
    reference: 2
    text: The left bank is steep. Turn the yoke gently right to reduce the bank,
      then ease the input.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1ef5e4e4f050b8b44bbfe5669ff390cd, type: 3}
  - cue: 3
    reference: 0
    text: The target heading is approaching. Roll gently left to level the wings,
      then center the turning input.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 95cf4b3861cb78e488d5e96feebdb672, type: 3}
  - cue: 4
    reference: 0
    text: The target heading is approaching. Roll gently right to level the wings,
      then center the turning input.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bd89871be00f7fe41a4c4a3b9d91d73e, type: 3}
  - cue: 5
    reference: 4
    text: Your target heading is to the left. Check outside, establish a shallow
      left bank, then watch the top index approach the target.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a4815dacfcc1b6841af43f66d44cb0fc, type: 3}
  - cue: 6
    reference: 4
    text: Your target heading is to the right. Check outside, establish a shallow
      right bank, then watch the top index approach the target.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e46bca7e70ce4746b2702018392cedf, type: 3}
  - cue: 7
    reference: 3
    text: You are low. Keep the wings nearly level and use a gentle climb toward
      the target. Check airspeed and add power if needed.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d74bd4937aef21f44a5622dfa5bcaa16, type: 3}
  - cue: 8
    reference: 3
    text: You are high. Use a gentle descent toward the target and monitor airspeed.
      Begin leveling before you reach it.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d87b3c622fd9fe94c84535e8354c3cb5, type: 3}
  - cue: 9
    reference: 1
    text: Airspeed is below the target. Ease an excessive nose-up attitude and add
      power as needed. Confirm the needle is recovering before continuing.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e8b73060832fca468448c2b5d46d88f, type: 3}
  - cue: 10
    reference: 1
    text: Airspeed is above the target. Reduce power a little and avoid an excessive
      nose-down attitude. Wait for the needle to respond.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2b6c4d73c04d8ab409f8ca5aa4e1ce93, type: 3}
  - cue: 11
    reference: 6
    text: The slip ball is left of center. Add a little left rudder with the right
      thumbstick, then ease it as the ball centers.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d256d82ca81fdb8408b9bdf9ad1f2a1b, type: 3}
  - cue: 12
    reference: 6
    text: The slip ball is right of center. Add a little right rudder with the right
      thumbstick, then ease it as the ball centers.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: df46ee5f4a499614b8f1b195f7d1a5d2, type: 3}
  - cue: 13
    reference: 11
    text: Taxi speed is high. Pull the throttle back and brake smoothly with both
      index triggers. Slow to a walking pace before turning.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 52c3ec557f55493419e44fbbebedee08, type: 3}
  - cue: 14
    reference: 11
    text: The stopping area is ahead. Close the throttle and apply both brakes gently.
      Keep the nose short of the runway.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3be499465c93d8c4c8ae072099042681, type: 3}
  - cue: 15
    reference: 7
    text: More power is needed for this task. Move the highlighted throttle forward
      smoothly and check airspeed and climb.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c4dc57bd20635ad409484d3cb290267f, type: 3}
  - cue: 16
    reference: 11
    text: Close the throttle to idle. Squeeze both index triggers together until
      the airplane is stopped.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 479d931d1e0408f4b90d47409ab15429, type: 3}
  - cue: 17
    reference: 8
    text: 'Check the current instruction: turning the yoke controls roll; pushing
      and pulling controls pitch. Use only the requested motion.'
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 02a99d6b83e2dac4796fdf839a891d86, type: 3}
  - cue: 18
    reference: 6
    text: Use the steering thumbstick sideways for rudder. Ease the input as the
      airplane points in the intended direction.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c89d54e60b3e70d4ebb298f1af6101e3, type: 3}
  - cue: 19
    reference: 10
    text: Hold the desired attitude first. Tap the trim thumbstick to trim, then
      ease the yoke input. Reverse trim direction if the correction grows.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4d474dac387988348b43c7366a1a89d3, type: 3}
  - cue: 20
    reference: 9
    text: The climb is established. Move the highlighted flap selector to ten degrees
      and confirm the indication.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: daacfe6c95db6da4aaa3af4eb888f2ab, type: 3}
  - cue: 21
    reference: 11
    text: The runway is off center. Correct early with a shallow turn. If a steep
      correction is needed close to the ground, go around.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9bc12a652bf2b31429be1cf87f5bdfa8, type: 3}
  - cue: 22
    reference: 11
    text: Check runway alignment, the airspeed needle and the descent. If they cannot
      be stabilized safely, go around.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bce85e1c9b7acc249b8268fb0a503b7a, type: 3}
  - cue: 23
    reference: 7
    text: Go around. Apply full power, carb heat cold, and a controlled climb attitude.
      Retract flaps in stages as the climb becomes established.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8feb4558b18b64145b6a9b8f93f16183, type: 3}
  - cue: 24
    reference: 0
    text: That correction has settled. Continue the current task and return your
      scan outside.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 43fbc5e901d14e4439061a55395fa781, type: 3}
  - cue: 25
    reference: 8
    text: Turn the yoke left. This check is a turning motion, not a push or pull.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 96303adadbf63224fa038183d8aa4e97, type: 3}
  - cue: 26
    reference: 8
    text: Left checked. Now turn the yoke right.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b054c60526bdc4342926034f3f223f20, type: 3}
  - cue: 27
    reference: 8
    text: Both turning directions are checked. Return the yoke to the middle and
      hold it there.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6dad2693ce6e8654596dd5825190af23, type: 3}
  - cue: 28
    reference: 8
    text: Push the yoke away from you. Keep it centered left to right.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1706e885b830008468656c85cdd47ec5, type: 3}
  - cue: 29
    reference: 8
    text: Forward checked. Now pull the yoke toward you.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6d9b2d938d3492d42918aad63fd69170, type: 3}
  - cue: 30
    reference: 8
    text: Both pitch directions are checked. Return the yoke to its middle position.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2d3b4cae86a59034d99989d9aa33fbc2, type: 3}
  - cue: 31
    reference: 6
    text: Move the steering thumbstick left.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e499186aac10502449144fd83c870f40, type: 3}
  - cue: 32
    reference: 6
    text: Left checked. Move the steering thumbstick right.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c0a22b359528dc54fa52358ce6dcd242, type: 3}
  - cue: 33
    reference: 6
    text: Both steering directions are checked. Let the steering thumbstick return
      to center.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 727a1d34e67a9f54fa1bb0d6314770cb, type: 3}
  markers:
  - reference: 0
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: Look through the windshield at the distant horizon, where sky meets
      terrain. Use it to judge pitch and bank; briefly cross-check the instruments,
      then look outside for traffic again.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e52158c0a5ff9cc40bcffe865cdda850, type: 3}
  - reference: 2
    marker: {fileID: 4425453207326071263}
    explanation: Find the round blue-and-brown instrument in the upper center of
      the main gauge group. Its fixed miniature airplane is your reference; the artificial
      horizon moves behind it. Compare it with the outside horizon.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7653e712d7115f74f9032faf28cf8160, type: 3}
  - reference: 1
    marker: {fileID: 5092024740439860943}
    explanation: Find the round dial with colored arcs, left of the blue-and-brown
      attitude instrument. Its needle reads speed through the air in knots, not taxi
      speed over the ground. Use the target in the current instruction.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: aff7196ea0dc7d04283a2c4b8b929121, type: 3}
  - reference: 3
    marker: {fileID: 4000679654135065730}
    explanation: Find the round multi-hand dial to the right of the attitude instrument.
      Its number window and hands show altitude in feet above sea level. Read the
      whole altitude, not only the fast-moving hundreds hand.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 57fae532dfbf490468dc197f2aac8579, type: 3}
  - reference: 4
    marker: {fileID: 787841819118726404}
    explanation: Find the rotating compass-card dial below the attitude instrument.
      Read the fixed index at the top; 9 means 090 degrees. This simulator uses true
      heading here, so use this highlighted dial for lesson targets.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9a299125aa342b642a10fbc55b79b68b, type: 3}
  - reference: 5
    marker: {fileID: 4439288029712437313}
    explanation: Find the round vertical-speed dial below the altimeter. Zero means
      level; the needle shows climb or descent in feet per minute. It lags attitude
      changes, so wait for the trend instead of chasing the needle.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a3225b1be009755499b61aa79b3f7e18, type: 3}
  - reference: 6
    marker: {fileID: 1206341969298665581}
    explanation: Find the small ball in the curved tube at the bottom of the turn
      instrument. Center it with gentle rudder toward the displaced ball. The right
      thumbstick supplies rudder input in this simulator.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e6be9d8ba9364b46837a5c139205555, type: 3}
  - reference: 7
    marker: {fileID: 4304181155796354961}
    explanation: Find the highlighted throttle knob below the instrument panel. Hold
      a grip over it and move it forward for more power, back for less. Identify
      this knob by its highlight before moving it; do not confuse it with mixture.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 10afa75edbca51443baae86ab85b10d2, type: 3}
  - reference: 8
    marker: {fileID: 4300490960307867227}
    explanation: The two-handled control in front of your seat is the yoke. Turning
      it left or right changes bank. Pushing it away or pulling it toward you changes
      pitch. Hold a controller grip to move it. These are two different motions.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a678192489542734b9293c22a37495dc, type: 3}
  - reference: 9
    marker: {fileID: 5864090527383306501}
    explanation: Find the highlighted flap selector beside the center controls. Move
      it to the required detent and confirm the flap indication. For these lessons,
      slow below eighty-five knots before extending flaps. Use each indicated position,
      not an estimated lever movement.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 803aa3af0648a7b4696aba5e1eab0106, type: 3}
  - reference: 10
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: Trim reduces the yoke input needed to hold an established attitude.
      During flight, tap the trim thumbstick up or down slightly and ease the held
      yoke input. Reverse the trim direction if the correction grows. Set attitude
      and power first; there is no force feedback.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 11493793927912346a949ba47c0e089f, type: 3}
  - reference: 11
    marker: {fileID: 0}
    explanation: Look outside for the paved runway, its centerline and edges. The
      elevated marker identifies the current practice area. Taxi only on the taxiway
      and stop before the runway entry; the marker is a teaching aid, not a clearance.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3629e726067530844bc4730779ff57a7, type: 3}
  worldMarker: {fileID: 3661077398707941412}
  worldMarkerPulse: {fileID: 2501880960978424173}
